WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.960
I'm off!

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.170
My summer vacation filled with lots of fun
and weirdness has ended.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:10.500
And now the new school semester begins.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.790
Doki doki wa kore kara!

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:33.710
Kiseki okoru yokan

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:40.960
Henachoko sajikagen de ii desho iza susume!

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:43.920
Ichika bachika yukeru donna basho datte

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:48.630
Motto kikasete core no oto made

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:53.420
Futari te o awasetara kowaku nai yo

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.790
Komatta toki ni wa

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.170
Omoidashite

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:01.920
Kimi ga iru tte koto

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.580
Onaji sora futari de miagete

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:13.960
Waraiatte tsurai koto mo norikoechaou

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:19.210
Dareka no tame ni ganbaru koto

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.750
Sore mo warukunai

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.380
Kyou mo tonari de

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:33.460
Tokimeki wa kore kara!

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:46.040
<b>NEW SEMESTER!</b>

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:46.040
<b>THE MAGICAL GIRL'S NEW DUTY!</b>

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:51.170
I'm worried about doing my
transfer student introduction to the class.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:54.250
Explaining the nature of my curse
will probably scare everyone away...

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:57.790
I have an idea, why don't you do it
while hugging your Mikansy doll?

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.210
Or if you'd like, I'll grab some pom-poms
and cheer for you from behind.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:01.080
Wazzup y'all?

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:05.210
<b>Mikansy</b>

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:01.920
Yay! Yay!

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:05.210
<b>Yay~</b>

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:05.210
<b>Yay~</b>

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.920
No, I'm pretty sure that would
just freak everybody out even more.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:05.210
<b>Booooo</b>

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.040
Booooo.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:06.080
Mikan.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:09.210
It's all right. Everyone will be glad to have you.

00:02:09.210 --> 00:02:13.210
Yeah, I'm already super happy and super excited
that you're going to be part of my class starting today!

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:16.920
That's really touching and all,
but you're just activating my curse!

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:22.580
Oh no! Oh no! Oh no!

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:20.830
Oh right, I forgot that making you
too happy also triggers the curse.

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:22.670
<b>BOW WOW</b>

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:21.830
You okay, Shamiko?

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:22.580
Quit it.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.170
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.170
<b>HINATSUKI</b>

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:27.170
I'm Mikan Hinatsuki and I'm a magical girl.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:33.540
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:33.540
<b>HINATSUKI</b>

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:28.880
It's wonderful to meet you all.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.500
Ms. Hinatsuki had an accident when she was very young
and it left her with a certain condition.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:38.540
Whenever she gets agitated, a protective magical power
that's inside of her will arbitrarily activate

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.170
and cause minor calamity for whoever is nearby her.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.210
<b>FU FU FU</b>

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:40.960
Fu, fu, fu, fu, fu...

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:48.380
You should all be aware that the triggers for her curse
include an elevated heart-rate and any sort of injury.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.830
My condition may seem like a hassle,
but I'll do everything I can to keep it under control!

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:55.580
Any pranksters in the class who might try
to surprise her should consider themselves warned.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:57.290
Aw man, no surprises?

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:59.420
Then when are we doing the celebratory party poppers?

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:01.460
We're not, Anri! Just put that away!

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:04.790
Okay, class. Does anybody have a question
for Ms. Hinatsuki?

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:08.290
I'm happy to talk about my curse and
my magical girl exploits, so feel free to ask me anything.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.250
Do you prefer having your fried eggs with salt,
soy sauce, or something else on top?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.080
Are you the type who eats
deep-fried foods in the morning?

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.710
Where do you start washing your body in the bath?

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.040
I wasn't expecting questions
that ignore the fantasy factor!

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.500
Um, so...

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:23.880
It's honestly okay if you want to ask for more details
about my condition and stuff.

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.920
I actually think it's best for everyone to be fully aware...

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:29.460
How exactly does that strange ribbon
on your head work?

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:33.290
It's something that grew out of my ether body,
so I can move it around depending on my mood!

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.170
Let's stop with softball questions like that, shall we?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:34.960
Dazzle!

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.250
<b>DAZZLE</b>

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.500
<b>DURING RECESS</b>

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:39.500
Shamiko!

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:44.420
<b>CITRUS</b>

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:41.250
Do you think my introduction was okay?

00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:43.210
It was the best one I've ever seen!

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:44.420
A citrus fan?

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:48.130
<b>CITRUS</b>

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:46.960
Quit playing around with the Whachamacallit Rod!

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.040
I'm showing my support!

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:52.040
So, you moved here to protect Shamiko?
You must be a hard worker!

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.500
Thanks! I'd love to swap contact info with you, Sata.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.500
Sure thing! And you can call me Anri!

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.290
That shaking thing they do to exchange info looks fun.
I wanna get a smart phone.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:04.330
Poke, poke, poke, poke, poke, poke.

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.330
I also think it would be a good idea for you
to get a phone, Shamiko.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:04.880
Slide, slide, slide.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:06.040
But they're expensive, aren't they?

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:09.040
Well, I can modify Ms. Lilith
with a phone function for totally free!

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:10.880
<b>HEY!!</b>

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:10.790
Stop, Ogura. That's a yellow card.

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:14.500
Are you going to join a club? I recommend
the tennis club! C'mon, let's play tennis!

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:16.380
I appreciate the thought, but...

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:22.830
since we magical girls have enhanced physical abilities,
it wouldn't be fair to play sports against regular humans.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:23.920
Oh.

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.580
That makes sense, I know Momochiyo is really powerful.

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:27.580
But actually...

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:28.960
wouldn't that be cool to see?

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:30.960
An all-out tennis battle between magical girls?

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.170
Peachy-pink, space-time rupturing baaaaallll!

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:37.000
Yes! Yes! I wanna see that!

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.580
Momo! We're going outside!

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:39.500
Not happening.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.710
The ball would just get torn to shreds after one serve.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.830
Darn it! Why can't you dream like the rest of us!

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.500
<b>HARUMPH!</b>

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.170
Harumph!

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:46.330
This reminds me, it's almost time
for the school's Sports Day.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.750
I'm actually a member of the Sports Day Committee.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:51.670
We're gonna have the student body split into
red and white teams and then competes for points.

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:54.540
I'm curious, how fast can you magical girls
run the 50-meter dash?

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.790
In about 6 seconds.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:56.420
3 seconds.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:58.000
This demon can do it in 11.2!

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:58.960
Whoa, seriously?

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:04.210
<b>SION OGURA'S 50 METER DASH TIME</b>

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:04.210
<b>SUNLIGHT'S TOO BRIGHT</b>

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:04.210
<b>AND I HATE IT</b>

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:01.750
For me, uh... 11.4 seconds.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.210
Sunlight's too bright and I hate it.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.960
You should probably leave us magical girls
out of the competition.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:13.500
Aw, shucks. It's kind of a bummer that you won't be able
to join the fun after transferring to our school.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:18.460
Hey! Then why don't I just develop an elixir
that temporarily drains the power from magical girls?!

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.580
That sounds good!

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:19.500
<b>That sounds good!</b>

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.920
Ogura, that's two and now you're ejected!

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.790
Sorry, only kidding!
The real reason I came was to give you this!

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:26.920
It's a dark side stabilizer potion for Chiyoda!

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:27.710
How about that.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.670
Wait, "dark side stabilizer"?!

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:32.880
<b>GRIND          GRIND           GRIND           GRIND      </b>

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.830
This is what I made by using
that pink gem you found the other day.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:36.750
It's all thanks to Shamiko for graciously
providing me with such a wonderful ingredient!

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.580
I don't recall "graciously providing" anything.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:43.250
This will stop the reduction and excess discharge of
your magic power when going to the dark side, Chiyoda.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:44.630
Be sure to drink it when you have trouble.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:49.380
Thank you so much! I never dreamed that precious gem
would come back to me as something even better!

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:52.710
Hold up, I'm gonna drink this?
It doesn't even look like a drinkable size!

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:55.290
We both know that gem was just a stone,
what else did you put in this?

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.540
Make sure you crunch it up when you take it, okay?

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.830
Answer my question.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:02.170
The school-wide committee meetings scheduled for
today will now begin.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:05.380
All students, please make your way
to your committee's appointed meeting place.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.380
Gotta go, see you later.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:06.210
Later!

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.040
What's going on?

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:10.580
Our school has a rule that everybody
has to serve as a member of one of the committees.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.790
Oh, we had that rule at my old school, too.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:14.130
Hey, Teach!

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.580
Mikan hasn't picked a committee to join yet!

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:20.250
Where would you like to join, Ms. Hinatsuki?
You're free to choose.

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:22.500
We'd love to have you as part
of the Anatomical Model Polishing Committee!

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.960
The Malabar Spinach Cultivation Committee
could use another pair of hands!

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:28.250
Would you consider joining
the Zombie Survival Manual Creation Committee?

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:30.290
Does this school not have any normal committees?!

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:33.040
Our school allows students
to create their own committees

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:35.580
based around something they want to work on.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.460
That's why we have a fair number
of irregular committees as well.

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:39.790
That's a little too unrestricted!

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.330
I'm on the Health Committee!

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.420
It would be easier to have a friend with you.
Would you care to join me?

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:45.830
Uh...

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:49.420
I'm concerned that my curse might be a problem
when students who are hurt suddenly show up for help.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.830
Excuse me, Miss? Would it be okay
if I started a Mikan Cultivation Committee?

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.540
Mikans, eh? They are quite tasty!

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:56.500
And in C-son.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:58.790
<b>IN C-SON</b>

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.790
How long would it take for the fruit to grow?

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:00.500
About 4 or 5 years from a seedling...

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:04.040
They wouldn't be done before you graduate,
so I'm afraid your application is rejected.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.500
That's such a shame...

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:09.580
<b>I WANT TO BE A CITRIS FRUIT THAT BLENDS IN WITH THE CLASS</b>

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.210
I don't know what I should do.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:10.540
I'm actually a member of the Sports Day Committee.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:14.580
Excuse me!

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:19.250
Would you mind if I joined
the Sports Day Committee with you, Sata?

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:20.710
Huh? Are you sure?

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.500
We're really busy with lots of work to do right now.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:26.830
To be honest, I didn't invite you to join
because of how hard it is.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.130
It's okay. I happen to love events like that.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:33.170
And besides, you said it was a bummer that I
wouldn't be able to participate directly in Sports Day.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:35.540
Even if I can't join any of the athletic challenges,

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:39.500
I think I'll be able to become good friends with everyone
by helping out from behind-the-scenes.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:43.040
And since Sports Day is coming up fast,
I'm sure there must be a lot I can help with.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.750
So please let me work alongside you.

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:46.210
Sure! We'd love to have you!

00:07:46.210 --> 00:07:50.040
Wonderful. Would you mind talking to the leaders
of the group and make sure it's all right with them?

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:50.750
Roger that!

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.540
Good for you, Mikan!

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:54.420
Welcome aboard!

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:54.880
Thanks!

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.080
Be prepared because there's no escape now.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:08:03.920
<b>CLENCH...</b>

00:07:57.170 --> 00:08:01.080
We're gonna put that magical girl super strength of yours
to good use by having you help set up the venue!

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:03.710
It sounds like I may have bitten off
more than I can chew...

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.710
Are you finished with your meeting?

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:08.880
You waited for us?

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.420
Yes! My meeting ended early, so I stuck around.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:14.630
I wanted to be close by, so that I could rush in
to help if anything came up.

00:08:14.630 --> 00:08:18.630
I appreciate that. But Anri's been watching out for me
to make sure I didn't get lost or anything.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:19.920
That's Anri for you!

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:23.790
This reminds me of when we first met.
She actually helped me back then, too.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:27.630
My body was very frail until my horns grew in.

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:31.540
So when I came to school for the very first time,
I collapsed from exhaustion after getting shipwrecked.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:33.290
How do you get "shipwrecked" at school?!

00:08:33.710 --> 00:08:35.710
Oh yeah, that takes me back!

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:36.830
<b>NEW STUDENT</b>

00:08:35.880 --> 00:08:38.290
Hey, are you all right? Do you feel sick?

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:40.040
You're a new first-year, right?

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:45.960
Yes... I got lost... and then my throat
started to hurt... really bad...

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:49.580
Getting lost at school is such a cool story!
Wanna go to the Nurse's Office?

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.790
I want to attend the entrance ceremony... please.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.830
I think I'll start feeling better if I just sit down for a while...

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:57.920
Okay, then let me take you to the auditorium!

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:00.580
Taxi at your service! Hop aboard, young missy!

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:01.750
Thanks...

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.960
You need to fetch a teacher at times like these, okay?

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:06.170
I'm sorry, ma'am.

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:08.420
I remember thinking Anri was kind of an oddball.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.170
You've gotten so much healthier
compared to back then, Shamiko!

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:15.130
And your quipping skills have become top-notch!

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:17.880
I'd rather be praised for being strong
than being a good quipper!

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:22.710
It's strange how things work. My summer vacation
filled with tons of excitement came to an end...

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:26.960
and now my school life has gotten
much more lively compared to the first semester.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:32.040
I hope I can keep making progress a little at a time.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:36.040
On that note, what committee is Momo even on?

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:37.630
Oh, hey. You guys headed home?

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.500
What are you doing, Momo?!

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:42.710
I'm busy with committee duties.

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:43.420
What committee?!

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:44.790
The Get Surrounded by Cats Committee.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:45.830
How does that work?!

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:50.080
There weren't any committees that I wanted to join,
so I created my own work to do.

00:09:50.080 --> 00:09:52.710
Okay, but I don't think the school
considers that an essential job...

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:56.000
That's not true. It's a very important and necessary job.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:58.170
Then look at me in the eyes and explain why!

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:04.330
W-well by checking on the health of every single cat...
that lives in the area around the school...

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:07.670
I can indirectly check... on the peace of the town?

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:09.670
Oh please, I can tell you're lying to yourself.

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.080
Slacking is a no-no!

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:14.130
Momochiyo! You're gonna join us
on the Sports Day Committee starting tomorrow!

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:14.750
Nuh-uh.

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:16.460
You better go and let everyone know right now!

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:20.880
Don't give up, Momo! Think of a reason
that doesn't have so many holes in it next time.

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:17.750
Roger that!

00:10:18.170 --> 00:10:19.750
What? No way.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:33.380
We're in trouble.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:35.130
Yeah, big trouble.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:36.460
This is so not good!

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:38.170
Not good at all!

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:38.830
Oh no!

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.170
Oh no!

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.830
What's the problem, you two?

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:40.830
Oh no!

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:45.380
Sports Day is almost here, but we're not even close
to finished with the preparations.

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:49.540
Why does our school have to schedule Sports Day
right after summer vacation ends?

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.830
There's hardly any chance
to meet up over summer vacation

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:53.380
because everyone is busy with clubs or cram school.

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.960
I gotta say, summer vacation in high school
is way busier than I expected it to be!

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:57.960
I can relate!

00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:02.250
I haven't been able to get rid of this lingering exhaustion
ever since I defeated 30,000 ancestues.

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:04.290
You defeated 30,000 of what now?!

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:10.750
<b>SIGH...</b>

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:10.710
We're gonna have to stay late every day
to finish all the work that we need to do.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:14.250
Having you and Momochiyo join us
is such a huge help, Mikan.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:15.460
Don't mention it.

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:18.630
I'm actually having a lot of fun
hanging out with new people.

00:11:18.790 --> 00:11:21.960
I don't understand what I'm even doing here.
I wanna go home.

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:23.670
I wanna go home and bury my face in my cat's stomach.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:25.000
That's code for "I'm having fun, too!"

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:26.710
When I say September, you say...

00:11:26.710 --> 00:11:28.040
Rain? Is it rain?

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:29.540
Hot! It's gotta be hot!

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.790
<b>STAAAAARE</b>

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:30.250
Sweet potatoes.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:34.500
Oh, that's right. Momo is also going to be
helping with the Sports Day preparations.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.790
Sweet potatoes are yummy!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:34.500
You're right about that.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.500
That means both her and Mikan
will be getting home late today.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.250
You're right about that.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.710
They're yummy.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:37.500
They are yummy.

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:39.170
I wanna eat some.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:39.880
Same here.

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:44.210
Hey Anri! For no real reason at all,
I'm also going to help out!

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:41.170
<b>GRAB!!</b>

00:11:44.210 --> 00:11:46.420
This Demon Girl will keep you company for the evening!

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:48.790
What got into you all of a sudden? But wow, thanks!

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:51.960
We're all part of the Sports Day Action Committee.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:53.460
We're first-years just like you!

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:55.580
<b>THE FIRST-YEAR MEMBERS OF THE SPORTS DAY ACTION COMMITTEE</b>

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:54.500
Nice to meet you.

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:55.580
I hope we can get along.

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:57.630
Y-yeah, same here.

00:11:57.880 --> 00:12:02.380
Getting straight to business, the tasks we're assigned
that haven't been finished yet are making the props,

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:04.080
and setting up the equipment.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:05.920
We also need to run simulations of the events.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:07.880
I see! So there's a lot of work to be done!

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:11.040
Bounce, bounce, bounce!

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:09.540
<b>BOUNCE</b>

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:10.290
<b>BOUNCE</b>

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:11.130
<b>BOUNCE</b>

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:11.750
<b>BOUNCE</b>

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:14.460
Hiyah! Kiyah! Yaaah!
Bounce, bounce, bounce...<b></b>

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:14.460
Let me know when the bread is at the right height.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:12.540
<b>BOUNCE</b>

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:13.250
<b>BOUNCE</b>

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.000
<b>BOUNCE</b>

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:14.710
<b>BOUNCE</b>

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:15.080
HIYAH!

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.080
HIYMMPH!

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:19.960
Okay, so we'll do 135 centimeters
for the bread-eating contest.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:22.920
Uh, I'd love a bite of that bread, too...

00:12:23.170 --> 00:12:25.670
Oh! But I think it would be better
to test on someone else!

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:28.460
Mikan! Will you swap jobs with me
and run the simulations?

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:31.670
All the Sports Day events will be
way too easy if they set them up based on me!

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.670
Sure, I'm all over it!

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:35.380
Thank you.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:37.130
Um, what else is there to do?

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:40.170
We were just talking about needing
to make the sashes for the relay.

00:12:40.170 --> 00:12:47.790
<b>ZIP ZIP ZIP ZIP ZIP</b>

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:43.790
I'll have those done in a jiffy!
Go help with something else!

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:47.790
Zip, Zip, Zip, Zip, Zip...

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:45.290
Those are godlike sewing skills!

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:47.790
I learned from making all those doll vessels for Ms. Lilith.

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:49.750
<b>RED</b>

00:12:48.210 --> 00:12:49.750
<b>TEAM</b>

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:56.750
<b>RED</b>

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:56.750
<b>TEAM</b>

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:52.170
Is it just me or are you kind of enjoying this?

00:12:52.170 --> 00:12:54.750
Absolutely not. I want this to be over with already.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:56.750
You say that, but the embroidery on these
is way too elaborate...

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:00.170
One, two! Three, four!

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.670
Mikan looks like she's having fun. I'm glad!
One, two! Three, four!<b></b>

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:04.460
Mikan is so cool, huh?

00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:07.710
Yeah, she's so stylish.
And the way she runs is so graceful!

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:09.500
Somebody's getting popular!

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:13.630
She's a very caring and charming person,
so obviously she's going to be popular.

00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:16.960
Yeah, but despite her lack of charm
you're totally on Team Momo, aren't you?

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:19.750
What the heck does that mean?!
I'm not on anybody's team!

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:23.040
But, personally, I think Momo has
her own unique charms.

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:26.000
How's it going, Mikan? Everything okay?

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.710
Oh, yes. Why are you so red in the face, Shamiko?

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:29.830
It's nothing.

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:34.500
I'm relieved to have found something to do at school.
I should be able to fit in now.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:35.830
W-well, that's good to hear.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:39.210
Listen, you don't need to worry about me
as much as you have been lately.

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:41.080
This town is easy to live in.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:44.960
There are a lot of strange and easy-going people in it,
but they're all very accepting.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.630
Living alone has its perks, too. I'm glad I made the move.

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:50.290
So, let's be clear.

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:50.960
<b>SMACK!!</b>

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:54.080
I had many reasons to transfer here
besides just protecting you!

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.880
I came because I wanted to!

00:13:56.630 --> 00:13:58.830
So please stop all your worrying, okay?

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:01.830
R-right!

00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:03.670
I need some help over here if anybody's free!

00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:05.670
We're going to put the finishing touches on our sign!

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:06.630
Coming!

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:08.080
Amazing!

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:11.130
<b>FIRST-YEAR</b>

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:11.130
<b>FELLOWSHIP</b>

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:10.960
This sign will be hung on the wall
out in the school yard, so it's gotta be big!

00:14:11.170 --> 00:14:14.710
We spent so long coming up with ideas
that we've totally fallen behind schedule, whoopsies!

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:16.670
We wanted to make something high-quality!

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:19.210
That's why we put love into every step of the process!

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.130
Those sound like excuses for taking too long...

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.960
Whoa, Chiyoda! You're really good at painting!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:34.830
Zip, zip, zip, zip, zip, zip...

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:25.670
I learned from making magic circles.

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:28.830
Well... I'm glad to see that Momo's having fun.

00:14:29.330 --> 00:14:30.750
Now to let it dry.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:32.330
Can I borrow this paint?

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.290
Okay, everybody stand up slowly.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:33.290
Go for it.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:37.460
So, Mikan, how does it feel riding on top?

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:40.080
I don't think this formation is very stable.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:43.830
For the event, it's probably safer if we form the legs
by only using students of similar heights.

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:44.880
Can you guys move?

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:45.580
I think so.

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:49.920
Are you okay, Mikan?!

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:51.710
Wait! Don't get close to her!

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:53.540
Whenever Mikan is unconscious, her curse is...

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:55.290
<b>DOOOOOM</b>

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:55.710
...at its most dangerous!

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:56.460
Get back!

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:20.080
<b>SECONDS</b>

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:28.710
Oh no, Mikan!

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:31.170
I think everything's okay now.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:33.380
Are you all right, Mikan?!

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.080
Y-yeah...

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.670
Yikes, the sign...

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.460
I'm so sorry.

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:41.040
You don't have to apologize, Mikan!

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:43.750
It's all my fault! I shouldn't have been moving
the paint without watching where I was going!

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.960
I'm also to blame for letting our formation fall apart!

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:47.960
Anyway, is your head doing okay?

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.460
You should cool down the spot
where you hit it with this frozen water bottle!

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.380
I was having trouble getting it to melt!

00:15:52.960 --> 00:15:54.250
I hope you're not hurt.

00:15:53.630 --> 00:15:54.960
We're sorry!

00:15:55.580 --> 00:15:56.500
Good work everyone!

00:15:56.500 --> 00:15:58.540
We should be able to finish everything at this rate!

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:01.580
It's time to call it a day. Look at how dark it's gotten!

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:03.380
See you tomorrow, Mikan. Okay?

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:04.630
Okay...

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:07.960
Shucks, I couldn't do anything.

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:10.080
But if it was possible...

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:13.500
Everything-Back-To-Normal Rod!

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:17.290
<b>GOOD</b>

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:17.290
<b>AS NEW</b>

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.420
There! Now the sign is as good as new!

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.080
<b>GRIP...</b>

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:22.420
It won't respond. I should've known.

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:25.790
I guess I still don't have enough power in the real world.

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:27.960
I'm going on ahead.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:31.040
Wait up, Mikan!

00:16:31.040 --> 00:16:34.540
Nothing that happened was your fault.
And nobody was bothered by it.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:38.290
Actually, I heard them saying
that it was exciting to see something so cool!

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:41.000
You know, the people of this town are really kind.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:43.920
You and Momo are two people I'm especially fond of.

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:47.830
And today, I grew to like everyone that I met at school.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:50.130
Then, let's go again tomorrow!

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:50.830
But...

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:56.170
It's the people who are kind, who get closest to me,
that end up getting hurt the most.

00:16:56.460 --> 00:17:00.580
The reason nobody got injured today was because
Momo just so happened to be there.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:03.000
Mikan, hear me out...

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.830
Keep your distance from me for today.

00:17:05.130 --> 00:17:08.920
I don't know what havoc my curse will wreak
if I get triggered now.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:11.960
And I would hate for anyone to get hurt... because of me.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:15.580
This power...

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:20.580
Originally, it was something
that was supposed to protect me from evil doers.

00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:25.460
And at first, I was even able to talk
with the little devil who got summoned.

00:17:26.460 --> 00:17:31.750
But my father didn't use a proper summoning ritual,
so things quickly started to go wrong.

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:37.290
I tried a few of my own ideas to mitigate it, but things
always end up like this when I let my guard down.

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:40.250
Mikan... let's talk more after you've calmed down.

00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:43.710
Yeah, good idea. I need some time to myself.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.290
Well, good night.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:56.420
That's okay.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:58.250
It was an emergency, right?

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:01.630
In return, I hope that you'll save me
whenever I get into trouble.

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:08.460
It doesn't really matter if I'm weak,
or dumb, or lack intuition!

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:11.830
Because there's something in this town
that only I can do!

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:16.330
Shamiko?
Momo?<b></b>

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:19.710
I was also just on my way to come and see you.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:22.420
It figures that we'd be on the same wavelength.

00:18:22.420 --> 00:18:24.170
You are my arch-nemesis after all!

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:26.880
Hey, Mikan!

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:27.830
Pardon us.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:31.000
Wh-what the heck? Don't you know better
than to barge into a lady's room!

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:34.290
Forget your room! Because we're about
to barge our way straight into your heart, okay?

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:34.290
Huh?!

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:38.040
I'm going to talk with the devil that's living inside of you,
so we can sort things out.

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:39.790
And my vassal is coming with me!

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:40.630
Yep.

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:42.080
WHAAAAAT?!

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:45.380
We're about to charge through your dreams
to enter your heart, Mikan.

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:46.130
Yep.

00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:47.460
B-but why...?

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:52.290
You mentioned you were able to talk
with the creature that's inside of you once before.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:55.170
Which made me think, maybe I could convince it
to stop causing trouble!

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:57.920
I think bringing a box of cakes
and some detergent will do the trick!

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.170
<b>INDOOR DRYING</b>

00:18:56.000 --> 00:18:58.170
<b>CHARAT</b>

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:00.130
Only if you were trying to convince
it to buy a newspaper subscription!

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:01.000
It could work!

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:02.380
Hold on, why is Momo going with you?

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:04.960
If Shamiko's plan fails, then I'll convince them by force!

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:07.880
Ugh, no! Cut the crap!
Momo is coming to serve as my bodyguard!

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:08.630
Bodyguard?

00:19:08.630 --> 00:19:10.880
Just how risky is what you're about to do, anyway?

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:12.380
Pretty risky, to be honest.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.670
We can get access to your heart without
any real problem as long as we have your blessing.

00:19:15.830 --> 00:19:19.080
But from the perspective of the devil inside of you,
we'd come off as invaders.

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:20.630
And there's no way of knowing how they'll react.

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:22.920
Then I don't see a reason for you to go through with this!

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:25.920
I've managed to live with my curse
just fine for years now!

00:19:25.920 --> 00:19:26.710
That's not acceptable!

00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:26.880
<b>CLENCH</b>

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:30.460
One of my duties as Shadow Mistress
is making sure that my minions are in good condition!

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:37.920
<b>ACCEPTING</b>

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:37.920
<b>ASSOCIATES!</b>

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:37.920
<b>Employee Benefits:</b>

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:37.920
<b>Dream Counseling</b>

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:37.920
<b>Home-cooked Meals</b>

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:37.920
<b>Your demonic employer will</b>

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:37.920
<b>Clean your room for you</b>

00:19:30.580 --> 00:19:33.500
I want my shadow organization to be attractive enough
that it gains many followers,

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:35.880
so I'll make it stand out by offering unique benefits!

00:19:36.040 --> 00:19:37.630
You sound like a venture capitalist...

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:41.790
Shamiko said that she wants to save you.
And I feel exactly the same.

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:45.290
It may be a little dangerous, but we want you
to have faith that we'll come back in one piece.

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:47.080
All right, then.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.250
Just promise me that you won't do anything extreme.

00:19:49.250 --> 00:19:51.040
Done! Let's get down to business!

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.790
Momo! It's time for the pitch-black potion!

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:55.790
Oh greaaaaat...

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:56.750
PB Potion!

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:58.250
SHLUUURP...

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:07.000
Chug! Chug! Chug! Chug!

00:19:58.250 --> 00:19:59.920
How is it? What's the flavor like?

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:07.040
<b>CHUG~ CHUG~</b>

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:02.000
Is it tasty? Go down smooth?

00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:04.290
It tastes like somebody boiled down garbage and mud...

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:05.170
I can't do this...

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:07.000
Aw, jeez! You're already going to extremes!

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:09.130
We're going to need as much information as we can get.

00:20:09.130 --> 00:20:12.130
What do you know about the creature
that's taken up residence inside of you, Mikan?

00:20:12.290 --> 00:20:15.040
Our family called it by the name "Ugallu."

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:16.920
That's one of Mesopotamia's beasts.

00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:19.290
Legends were passed down that it would
protect your home from the wicked

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:21.630
if you carved its appearance into the entrance.

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:23.670
But I doubt we're dealing with the real thing.

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:27.710
Because if it was truly the Ugallu of myth,
then it should be way more powerful.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:31.540
I bet your dad just used a magic familiar
that's capable of following a simple bodyguard routine

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:33.670
and affixed it to a vessel that looked similar to Ugallu.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:36.580
I see. Kinda like that black licorice monster.

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:38.380
What black licorice monster?

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:40.330
Something I got chased by once before...

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:44.790
Generally speaking, familiars
can only perform simple tasks

00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:46.540
and don't have any consciousness of their own.
Hey, hey!<b></b>

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:46.580
<b>HEY, HEY!</b>

00:20:47.040 --> 00:20:49.830
The problem with Ugallu was
that it used my magic as nourishment

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:52.500
to become something more complex
than any of us expected.

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:58.460
And, in the end, we lost control of it.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:00.330
My dad has nothing but regrets

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:01.830
Hey, hey! We want a pitcher, not a belly-itcher!

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.880
<b>Hey, hey! We want a pitcher,</b>

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.880
<b>not a belly-itcher!</b>

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:01.830
and I wish I could solve the problem myself.

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:06.130
Ugallu... it's hard to tell what kind of snacks
it might like based on the name alone, huh?

00:21:06.130 --> 00:21:07.670
I have a hunch it's a meat-eater.

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:07.830
<b>I have a hunch</b>

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:07.830
<b>it's a meat-eater</b>

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:11.330
Anyways, let's go and give it a try!

00:21:11.460 --> 00:21:14.380
Saddle up, because it is officially futon time, my friends!

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:13.330
Hey! Hey!

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.330
<b>HEY!</b>

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:13.330
<b>HEY!</b>

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:16.250
Everybody get into bed next to each other!

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:19.130
Are we sure that futon time is absolutely necessary?

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:23.000
It feels like Yuko has really grown into her own as of late.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:25.880
I'm gonna work hard to be a reliable advisor for her!

00:21:26.920 --> 00:21:29.670
Yuko... are you feeling hungry?

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:54.830
...ke up... wake up...

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:56.040
Wake up, Shamiko!

00:21:57.170 --> 00:21:57.880
Huh?

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:00.790
Looks like we got inside of Mikan's heart
without any problems.

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:02.920
It's pretty hard to see our surroundings.

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.960
Shamiko, you better stay close to me.

00:22:04.960 --> 00:22:07.290
Where'd you get that sword?! It's dope as all heck!

00:22:08.670 --> 00:22:10.670
Why are you getting so hysterical over it?

00:22:10.790 --> 00:22:12.630
Because it's straight up my demonic alley!

00:22:12.630 --> 00:22:14.380
Watch out, blades are dangerous!

00:22:12.630 --> 00:22:14.880
Let me take a look! Strike a pose with it!

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:16.420
Enough, just back off!

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:16.670
<b>SLASH</b>

00:22:16.630 --> 00:22:18.750
I'm sorry! I got too carried away!

00:22:19.290 --> 00:22:23.330
Don't give up, Shamiko!
Fight your battles in a way that only succubi can.

00:22:23.460 --> 00:22:25.380
I got too carried away!

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:46.710
Mata aeta ne drama nandatte? (howa howa)

00:22:46.710 --> 00:22:49.710
Sugu (sugu!) oshie ni mo icchauzo (utou!)

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:52.630
Kakyuuteki naruhaya de (saa!)

00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:55.250
Ara post mo "ohayou" nante (pikopiko)

00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:57.460
Mou shippo made saeteru (waa!)

00:22:57.460 --> 00:23:01.290
Hakusen o tondette itsu mentsudoeba

00:23:01.290 --> 00:23:04.040
Kyou mo hajimatteku

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:07.830
Totsuzen ni mystery

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:11.210
Kurakura mayou kedo

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:15.790
Te to te o tori doko made mo susume

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:22.670
Guruguru machi wa mawari kagayaku

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:25.580
Korokoro toehatae shite

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:28.290
Yume o mazeta yoikagen wa

00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:31.250
Kimi ni hana o sakaseru yo

00:23:31.250 --> 00:23:34.080
Yomo made kakomu tetragon

00:23:34.210 --> 00:23:37.040
Aa machikado ni hanataba

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:40.000
Nee ima wa mou sukoshi

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:44.040
Sottosotto sono hana o misete

00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:47.540
Yokubacchaeba mou ikkai

00:23:56.080 --> 00:24:10.920
<b>PREVIEW</b>

00:23:57.080 --> 00:23:59.330
It's so blurry, we can't see anything.

00:23:58.630 --> 00:23:59.330
Tummy-wummy.

00:23:59.330 --> 00:24:01.420
Momo. I need you to buy some more time.

00:24:00.330 --> 00:24:02.170
We can't afford to try more than once.

00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:04.000
Do you want me to give you some advice?

00:24:02.750 --> 00:24:04.000
We can't let things end like that!

00:24:04.170 --> 00:24:04.580
Absolutely no disappearing!

00:24:04.580 --> 00:24:05.210
I was forced to wear

00:24:05.210 --> 00:24:06.960
all those humiliating cosplays over and over...

00:24:06.080 --> 00:24:07.830
You're gonna start from scratch, got that?

00:24:07.040 --> 00:24:10.920
<b>A RITUAL IN DARKNESS! THE DEMON'S NEW ALLY!!</b>

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:08.790
I can't believe I let myself get distracted for a second.

00:24:08.790 --> 00:24:10.830
She's got it stuck in a full nelson...
